{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802299-the-invictus-have-the-best-servants","id":802299,"title":"The Invictus Have The Best Servants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-06T13:14:46-08:00","id":802299,"title":"The Invictus Have The Best Servants","content":"The Invictus are the best at Ghouls. The Vassal of an Oath doesn't have to be a Vampire, and some Oaths are <i>stupidly</i> good for Ghouls.<br /> <br /> <b>Oath of Action:</b> Very risky... but an <i>excellent</i> way of boosting a Ghoul. It also lets you share <i>any</i> Discipline you have, so you could theoretically hand a Ghoul Blood Sorcery if you belong to the right Bloodline.<br /> <br /> <b>Oath of Fealty:</b> Requires <i>exceptional</i> circumstances (you do need Invictus Status \u2022), but it's the <i>holy grail</i> of Blood Oaths for a Ghoul. It gives them a Vitae source that has <i>no</i> chance for Vitae Addiction or the Vinculum. Sure, it means their Liege automatically knows whether or not they are lying to them, but that's more-or-less fine. It's also good on the Vampire's end, since the Oath of Fealty is straight-up <i>better</i> than pretty much any other source of Vitae I can think of (as far as Ghouls are concerned.)<br /> <br /> <b>Oath of Penance:</b> <i>Great</i> for the Ghoul... terrible for you. There's a niche use with regards to dumping this on an <i>ally's</i> Ghoul, however. In exceptional (read: story related) circumstances, having the <i>Ghoul</i> be the liege and being the vassal can be <i>heavily</i> beneficial. Heavily.<br /> <br /> <b>Oath of Serfdom:</b> Hoo-boy. Give one of your Ghouls a &quot;feeding territory&quot; to take care of, and get a loyal watchdog that gets a free dot of a Physical Discipline when defending you. It <i>does</i> run into the issue of Ghouls not being able to <i>use</i> the Feeding Grounds merit, but...<br /> <br /> <b>Oath of the Safe Word:</b> Do you trust your Ghoul? I mean <i>really</i> trust them? Share your Invictus Status and Willpower with them. Then get them to swear an Oath of Fealty to you. This has the potential to go <i>very</i> wrong, but it can also go <i>very</i> right.<br /> <hr /><br /> The &quot;dream set-up&quot; is Oath of the Safe Word + Oath of Fealty + Oath of Action + Reversed Oath of Penance + Reversed Oath of Fealty. Assuming you have Invictus Status \u2022\u2022\u2022, that gives...<br /> <br /> <b>For The Ghoul:</b><br /> - Invictus Status \u2022\u2022\u2022 (shared via Oath of the Safe Word).<br /> - Can draw up to three Vitae from you a week.<br /> - Gets one out of every ten Vitae you drink.<br /> - Shares your Willpower pool.<br /> - Gets the <i>full</i> benefits of one of your Disciplines.<br /> - Automatically knows if you're lying to them.<br /> <br /> <b>For You:</b><br /> - A dot of Blood Potency.<br /> - Immunity to all of the Ghoul's Disciplines.<br /> - You can draw up to three Vitae from the Ghoul each week.<br /> - You share the Ghoul's Willpower pool.<br /> - You share one of the Ghoul's social merits.<br /> - You automatically know if the Ghoul is lying to you.<br /> <br /> <b>Stuff That Can Go Wrong:</b><br /> - If they complete the Oath of Action, you take Aggravated damage equal to the Discipline dots you granted the Ghoul.<br /> - They can call off the Oath of the Safe Word, paralysing you for a turn + 1 turn per Willpower spent.<br /> <br /> But why should any of that be a problem? You're supplying them with their sweet, sweet blood fix <i>and</i> power! Sure, all the other members of the Invictus are looking at you funny, but <i>nothing</i> in the city charter says that Ghouls cannot receive a pre-membership in the Invictus (probably because it never came up before)!<br /> <br /> Also, <i>seriously</i>, what did the Ghoul <i>do</i> to earn both your fealty <i>and</i> an apology?<br /> <hr /><br /> I think the takeaway here is that some Oaths have really interesting alternate uses if you flip the words &quot;liege&quot; and &quot;vassal&quot; in your head. I can see some Domains where these &quot;inverted&quot; uses are more common than the standard ones (a Vampire feudal system built around vassals giving their lord Feeding Grounds in exchange for permission to use it <i>and</i> the Lord being better able to defend them when push comes to shove would be... interesting. I might have to give that one some thought.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T02:48:55-08:00","id":802946,"title":"","content":"Ahem <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/800465-four-invictus-devotions/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...evotions/page2</a><br /> <br /> There's more reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T05:35:36-08:00","id":802997,"title":"","content":"Oath of Penance has a heavy drawback. I think you forgot that.<br /> <br /> &quot;While a vassal is paying penance, she may not gain the benefits of any other Oath. She retains their drawbacks.&quot;\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T08:59:59-08:00","id":803138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802299-the-invictus-have-the-best-servants?p=802997#post802997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oath of Penance has a heavy drawback. I think you forgot that.<br /> <br /> &quot;While a vassal is paying penance, she may not gain the benefits of any other Oath. She retains their drawbacks.&quot;\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw mang, I knew I missed that one.<br /> <br /> Fine, drop the Reversed Oath of Penance from the dream set-up. Still, a nice way to sabotage other people's Ghouls (if they are also doing the crazy oath shuffle.)<br /> <br /> As for the Devotions... I knew about them, but those are separate, you know? For the two Devotions that affect other people, they have restrictions more specific than &quot;member of the Invictus&quot;... and can be taken by people who <i>aren't</i> members. Therefore, they factor into why <i>Vampires</i> are good at minions, not just Invictus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:03:12-08:00","id":804491,"title":"","content":"So this makes me wonder what other Ghoul buffs exist. I know there is a devotion that let's someone use your Resilience.<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracule can give a Ghoul vampire senses and let them get a scene - long physical intensity at your blood potency","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T06:42:30-08:00","id":805203,"title":"","content":"I bet the Circle of the Crone Ghoul enhancing Devotions (if they exist) are extremely nasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T10:33:33-08:00","id":805344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802299-the-invictus-have-the-best-servants?p=805203#post805203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet the Circle of the Crone Ghoul enhancing Devotions (if they exist) are extremely nasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd look less at Devotions and more at Cruac. Something to awaken a Beast in a Ghoul would be... something.<br /> <br /> That being said, Theban Sorcery can make one of your Ghouls a genius with a one-dot spell, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T12:29:43-08:00","id":805401,"title":"","content":"Blood Sorcery in general is pretty horrific. And now I'm thinking of the Crone's Mantle (Not sure if that's the proper name) Ritual in the Secrets of the Convenants preview. If you suffer a wound penalty due to Aggravated damage from the effects of that ritual, the person so injured gains a dot of the Cruac Discipline. Could this include Ghouls and/or baseline humans? If so, perhaps instead of capping Humanity, dots in Cruac would cap Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T12:58:40-08:00","id":805418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802299-the-invictus-have-the-best-servants?p=805401#post805401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Sorcery in general is pretty horrific. And now I'm thinking of the Crone's Mantle (Not sure if that's the proper name) Ritual in the Secrets of the Convenants preview. If you suffer a wound penalty due to Aggravated damage from the effects of that ritual, the person so injured gains a dot of the Cruac Discipline. Could this include Ghouls and/or baseline humans? If so, perhaps instead of capping Humanity, dots in Cruac would cap Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing <i>stopping</i> it from doing so - I'd just say that they can't purchase more dots.<br /> <br /> And that seems reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:20:37-08:00","id":805627,"title":"","content":"Cruac requires you to spill Vitae, doesn't it? I'm pretty sure that means Ghouls can't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:01:23-08:00","id":805651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802299-the-invictus-have-the-best-servants?p=805627#post805627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cruac requires you to spill Vitae, doesn't it? I'm pretty sure that means Ghouls can't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't stop them from gaining Cruac, though.<br /> <br /> They just can't <i>use</i> it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:09:00-08:00","id":805991,"title":"","content":"In first edition, ghouls could learn both Cr\u00faac and Theban sorcery, though this was highly prohibited and often ended up with the execution of the regnant and ghoul. The book says that in order to spill the Vitae they would have to spill an equal amount of their own blood, in the form of Lethal damage. It points out that while the Vitae isn't in the blood, the nature of the ritual's demand for blood sacrifice is what empowers it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:13:26-08:00","id":806050,"title":"","content":"Ghouls, as per 1e, could use Cruac. In fact, there was an entire ghoul family devoted to it. There are a mortal family of Cruac practicioners in the Blood Sorcery book as well. Generally speaking, I'd argue that most vampires wouldn't TEACH a ghoul blood magic, but they'd be completely capable of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:38:16-08:00","id":806109,"title":"","content":"Ghouls could learn -any- discipline in 1e. They just stuck to the physical ones because why would you let blood addicts walk around without being seen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}